{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate CMPA training & fund specialised referral pathways in primary care",
        "additional_details": "Many families face months of delay, misdiagnosis, and dismissive care when seeking help for infants with Cow\u2019s Milk Protein Allergy (CMPA). Non-IgE (delayed) symptoms like severe reflux, blood in stool, skin flare-ups, and extreme distress can be written off as \"just colic\". Many parents experience lengthy trial-and-error formula changes without specialist support. We believe primary care teams need standardised training to recognise CMPA early and specialised pathways to refer infants to dietitians without delay.",
        "background": "Mandate standardised CMPA (Cow's Milk Protein Allergy) for all primary care staff and fund guaranteed, fast-tracked paediatric dietetic referral pathways. We want to end diagnostic delays, trial-and-error formula restrictions, and poor early intervention for infants with Cow\u2019s Milk Protein Allergy.",
